    "https://www.mercy.edu/about/human-resources/employment-mercy": {
      "title": "Employment",
      "description": "Employment at Mercy | Mercy University Skip to main site navigation Skip to main content Important Links Request Info Apply Visit Open the search panel Search Academics Majors & Programs School of Business School of Education School of Health & Natural Sciences School of Liberal Arts School of Nursing School of Social & Behavioral Sciences 4+1 Programs Mercy Online Learning Libraries Academic Centers Academic Support Catalogs, Bulletins, & Calendars Office of the Provost Research and Grants Special Programs Admissions & Aid Apply Now First-Time Freshman Admissions Transfer Admissions Graduate Admissions International Admissions Catalyst Program Events Financial Aid High School Programs Parents & Guardians School Counselor Resources Veterans Visit Campus Student Life Athletics Campus Locations Campus Safety Commuting to Mercy Dining at Mercy Residential Life Student Activities & Organizations Student Stories Student Support CARE Team Career Development Counseling Services Hazing Prevention and Response Health & Wellness Center International Student Services Mavs RESPONSE Office of ACCESSibility Office of the Registrar Opportunity Programs PACT Smoke Free Policy Transcript Requests About Awards & Accreditations Office of the President Board of Trustees Hispanic-Serving Institution Human Resources Job Opportunities at Mercy Information Technology Mercy Administrative Center Our History Support Mercy Welcome to Mercy University Directory Contact Us Programs Athletics Blackboard Mercy Connect News & Events Give Jobs Information For... Current Students Alumni Faculty International Students Job Seekers Parents & Families School Counselors CNR Alumni Employment at Mercy About Mercy The Office of Human Resources Employment at Mercy Become A Maverick Join Us and Make an Impact Working at Mercy University means becoming part of an institution that not only values your expertise but also invests in your future. Whether you’re contributing to academic excellence, advancing research, supporting student success or driving innovative solutions, your work will have a lasting, meaningful impact. We invite you to join a community that is committed to growth, inclusion and service. At Mercy University, your career isn’t just a job – it’s a pathway to personal fulfillment, professional achievement and the chance to shape a brighter future for generations to come. Current Positions Part-Time & Full-Time Staff Adjunct & Full-Time Faculty Campus Employment See All Positions Why Mercy? At Mercy University, we don’t just educate – we inspire, innovate, and lead.  As a prospective employee, you would join a vibrant, mission-driven institution that is shaping the future of higher education and making a lasting impact on students, communities and the world. We believe that our strength lies in our people. From faculty to staff, we cultivate an inclusive, dynamic, and supportive workplace where every voice is valued, every contribution is recognized, and everyone has the chance to thrive. We are committed to fostering an environment where creativity, collaboration and innovation flourish and where your professional journey is nurtured every step of the way. Working at Mercy Mercy University actively recruits a diverse workforce and student body that includes members of historically underrepresented groups, and strives to build and sustain a welcoming and supportive campus community. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, marital status, religion, sex, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. Mercy University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer/M/F/Veteran/Disability People applying for more than one position need to provide application material for each position. Some positions require skills or other proficiencies where a demonstration of these skills is conducted at the University. All applications should be submitted through our applicant portal. Potential employees and applicants are invited to review our Annual Security Report.  The Annual Security Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning specific reported crimes that occurred on campus and on public areas within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus. These statistics are compiled from campus incident reports, reports from designated Campus Security Authorities, and from local police departments. Statistics related to fires that may have occurred in on-campus student housing are included as part of this report.  The report also describes institutional policies relevant to campus security. For more information, please click here . Screening & Procedures Should you decide to apply to Mercy University, your application will be screened and we will respond to all applicants who meet the minimum requirements of the job for which they are applying. If you have questions, or if you are experiencing technical difficulty, please contact us at hr@mercy.edu . Applicants and employees of most private employers, state and local governments, educational institutions, employment agencies and labor organizations are protected under Federal law from discrimination. Find out more, here . Mercy University Employee Benefits Overview At Mercy University, we are committed to providing a comprehensive and competitive benefits package that supports your well-being, professional development and work-life balance. Below is an overview of the benefits available to employees: Health & Wellness Coverage: Mercy offers a variety of medical plans, including options with UnitedHealthcare Oxford and Emblem Health, prescription drug coverage, dental and vision care. You also have access to wellness programs and gym reimbursements to support your physical health. Generous Paid Time Off: Mercy’s paid time off benefits include vacation days, sick leave, holidays, personal days and winter break. These generous time-off options ensure that you have the time to rest and recharge while also managing family and personal responsibilities. Retirement & Financial Planning: Mercy University provides a robust retirement plan, with contributions based on your age and length of service. In addition, employees have access to flexible spending accounts (FSA), helping you save pre-tax dollars for medical, dependent care and commuter expenses. Employee Assistance Programs: Mercy’s Employee Assistance Program (EAP) provides confidential support for you and your family, including counseling for personal, family and work-related issues, financial and legal guidance and mental health resources. Work-Life Balance: Mercy University understands the importance of balancing your career with personal life. That’s why we offer flexible work schedules, remote work opportunities and hybrid work arrangements where possible. Professional Development & Growth: Mercy University is committed to supporting your career development with access to various training programs, workshops and conferences. Tuition Remission: Employees and their immediate families benefit from tuition remission programs, allowing you to pursue undergraduate and graduate studies at Mercy University at a reduced cost. Life Insurance & Disability Protection: Mercy University offers life insurance coverage, along with short- and long-term disability benefits, to provide financial protection for you and your loved ones in case of unforeseen events. Upwards Care Navigator: Your Care Navigator through Upwards is a personal assistant tool to help research, tour and enroll your children in affordable and quality licensed early childhood education and care programs. Employee Discounts: Employees are able to access exclusive discounts on university services, local businesses and major retailers, enhancing your lifestyle and supporting your day-to-day needs. Mercy's Workplace Culture Working at Mercy University is about much more than the work.  As our mission declares and our employees will tell you: IT’S A CALLING. Our Mission: “Mercy University is committed to providing motivated students the opportunity to transform their lives through higher education by offering liberal arts and professional programs in personalized and high quality learning environments, thus preparing students to embark on rewarding careers, to continue learning throughout their lives and to act ethically and responsibly in a changing world.” Getting to Campus Dobbs Ferry Campus Bronx Campus Manhattan Campus Employment Information Every Mercy University employee, from facilities to the athletic fields to the lecture halls, is “consumed in service” as our motto shows. They are deeply invested in the promise of higher education and its importance to the population of students we serve – primarily first-generation, low-income students for whom college might not be in the cards but for Mercy. Working at Mercy, you can weave your individual contribution within a larger tapestry of diversity and equity in student success that will impact generations of families immediately and into the future. Take The Next Step We believe if colleges were more open, people's minds would be more open, too. Because if all kinds of students got degrees, all kinds of people would have new opportunities. And with every new opportunity, the world transforms. Not every institution believes in this vision, but we do. The world isn't made for Mavericks, but Mercy is. Come join us. Plan a Visit Request Information Apply Now Have Questions? Call 1.877.MERCY.GO A Thriving Community After Graduation Join more than 70,000 graduates from Mercy University and the College of New Rochelle in networking and support future generations of students with a gift. Mercy Alumni CNR Alumni Make a Gift Academics Admissions & Aid Campus Life Student Support About Contact Visit Libraries Campus Safety Bookstores Success Toolkit Career & Professional Development Apply Directory Campus Maps Work @ Mercy Service Excellence Student Achievement Westchester 555 Broadway Dobbs Ferry, NY 10522 (914) 674-7600 Manhattan 47 West 34th St New York, NY 10001 (877) 637-2946 Bronx 1200 Waters Place Bronx, NY 10461 (718) 678-8899 ©2026 Mercy University Title IX Consumer Information Mercy University Policies NC-SARA Whistleblower Policy Human Resources Information Technology Privacy Policy Strategic Plan Powered by Google Translate"
    },
    "https://www.mercy.edu/about/human-resources/employement-mercy": {
