hat you have the time to rest and recharge while also managing family and personal responsibilities. Retirement & Financial Planning: Mercy University provides a robust retirement plan, with contributions based on your age and length of service. In addition, employees have access to flexible spending accounts (FSA), helping you save pre-tax dollars for medical, dependent care and commuter expenses. Employee Assistance Programs: Mercy’s Employee Assistance Program (EAP) provides confidential support for you and your family, including counseling for personal, family and work-related issues, financial and legal guidance and mental health resources. Work-Life Balance: Mercy University understands the importance of balancing your career with personal life. That’s why we offer flexible work schedules, remote work opportunities and hybrid work arrangements where possible. Professional Development & Growth: Mercy University is committed to supporting your career development with access to various training programs, workshops and conferences. Tuition Remission: Employees and their immediate families benefit from tuition remission programs, allowing you to pursue undergraduate and graduate studies at Mercy University at a reduced cost. Life Insurance & Disability Protection: Mercy University offers life insurance coverage, along with short- and long-term disability benefits, to provide financial protection for you and your loved ones in case of unforeseen events. Upwards Care Navigator: Your Care Navigator through Upwards is a personal assistant tool to help research, tour and enroll your children in affordable and quality licensed early childhood education and care programs. Employee Discounts: Employees are able to access exclusive discounts on university services, local businesses and major retailers, enhancing your lifestyle and supporting your day-to-day needs. Mercy's Workplace Culture Working at Mercy University is about much more than the work.  As our mission declare