    "https://talenthub.mercy.edu/jobs/search?page=1&employment_type_uids%5B%5D=16d59ca21b920b9e57edce4782724083&employment_type_uids%5B%5D=ea51d2e7eee4b3544e5852c3006c9b82&query=": {
      "title": "With Every Opportunity the World Transforms",
      "description": "Search Page About Mercy Why Mercy (current) Mercy in the News View All Jobs My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode With Every Opportunity the World Transforms Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 10 filter options found Category Adjunct (0 items) 0 Admissions (5 items) 5 Athletics/Coaching (10 items) 10 Campus Employment (0 items) 0 Faculty (2 items) 2 Higher Education (0 items) 0 Information Technology (2 items) 2 Library (2 items) 2 Management (2 items) 2 Staff (43 items) 43 Department Search departments 21 filter options found Department Admissions & Recruitment (14 items) 14 Athletics (9 items) 9 Center for Student Success (1 items) 1 Faculty Development (0 items) 0 Grants (0 items) 0 Information Technology (2 items) 2 Institutional Advancement (4 items) 4 Libraries, Inst Tech & Online Learn (2 items) 2 Marketing & Communication (1 items) 1 Office of Student Financial Service (1 items) 1 Operations and Facilities (2 items) 2 Provost's Office (4 items) 4 School of Business (0 items) 0 School of Education (2 items) 2 School of Health & Natural Sciences (3 items) 3 School of Liberal Arts (1 items) 1 School of Nursing (3 items) 3 School of Social & Behavorial Sci (0 items) 0 Student Clubs Assoc Activities (0 items) 0 Student Services Support Center (1 items) 1 Student Srvs Auxiliary (0 items) 0 Employment Type Search employment types 5 filter options found Employment Type Faculty Full-time (3 items) 3 Faculty Part Time (0 items) 0 Staff Full-time (32 items) 32 Staff Part-Time (19 items) 19 Student worker (0 items) 0 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Baseball Coach- BB3720 492707 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University's baseball program is looking for a dedicated Assistant Baseball Coach to join its Athletics staff at the Dobbs Ferry campus. If you're ready to invest in student-athletes both on the field and in the classroom, this is a role where your coaching expertise genuinely shapes lives. Read more Learning Support Manager- A00744 492709 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Staff Full-time The Learning Support Manager for the Center for Academic Excellence and Innovation (CAEI) provides coordination and oversight of academic support services designed to enhance student learning, persistence, and academic success. Reporting to the CAEI Director, the Learning Support Manager is responsible for managing tutoring operations, developing and supporting peer tutors, faculty tutors, and strengthening partnerships with faculty, academic departments, and student success teams.\nThe Learning Support Manager serves as a campus leader for academic support by ensuring students have access to high-quality, proactive, and inclusive learning resources. This position supports CAEI’s mission to promote independent learning, increase utilization of tutoring services, improve student outcomes in high-need courses, contributing to institutional retention and on-time graduation. Read more Assistant Director of Student Financial Services- A00217 492710 Manhattan, New York, United States Office of Student Financial Service Staff Staff Full-time Under the direction of the Senior Assistant Director of Student Financial Services, the Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will assist in the management of the daily operations of the Student Financial Services Offices to support the Campus Operations ensuring the professional, efficient and compliant processing of student records.  The Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will assist in the management of the supervision of registration processes, resulting billing processes, and counseling of students and families.  The Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will also serve as a primary supervisor of the Student Financial Services Counselors, ensuring student centered service in meeting the needs of traditional, non-traditional, adult and minority student populations. Read more Women's Flag Football Assistant Coach- WF3700 492711 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University Athletics is building something real on the flag football field, and the right assistant coach will be part of it from the ground up. If you know the game, connect with student-athletes, and want to contribute to a program that competes with purpose, this is your opportunity. Read more Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions- A00307 492685 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Admissions Staff Staff Full-time The Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions supports the Associate Director and Director of Graduate Admissions in achieving enrollment goals across Mercy’s graduate programs. This role focuses on implementing recruitment and admissions initiatives, supervising staff, managing a defined recruitment territory, and cultivating relationships with prospective students, community partners, and academic departments. The Assistant Director contributes to process improvements, supports yield and communication efforts, and represents Mercy at events to expand graduate enrollment and strengthen partnerships. Read more Executive Director, Academic Success and Accessibility (A00736) 492652 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Staff Faculty Full-time Staff Full-time The Executive Director for Academic Success and Accessibility serves as a senior academic leader responsible for advancing an integrated, student-centered model of academic support and accessibility services across Mercy. Reporting to the Senior Vice Provost for Academic Affairs, the Executive Director provides strategic leadership for accessibility services, tutoring, learning support initiatives, early alert interventions, and student success programs designed to improve retention, persistence, academic achievement, and degree completion. Read more Associate Director, Corporate & Foundation Relations- A00743 492704 Tarrytown, New York, United States Institutional Advancement Staff Staff Full-time The Assistant/Associate Director, Corporate & Foundation Relations will support the goals of the Executive Director for Corporate & Foundation Relations (ED CFR) in support of institutional priorities through prospect research and development of letters of interest, proposals, and grant applications. The position will assist in growing the donor population through discovery, qualification and solicitation. The position assists in the management of donor stewardship and engagement which includes preparing door impact reports, and pre- and post-award contract compliance. Read more Library Assistant- C00044 492667 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Libraries, Inst Tech & Online Learn Library Staff Full-time Mercy University Libraries’ is seeking self-motivated, energetic, and detail-oriented candidates to fill a patron centered support role within the Dobbs Ferry Campus Circulation team. Reporting to the Associate Director, the position’s primary duties will include supervising library circulation and reserve operations, assisting students and faculty with library resources and related technology needs. The Library Assistant will collaborate with branch circulation supervisors, the systems librarian, and reference librarians. Additionally, the position will monitor front desk inquiries, library computers, printers, and software resources and support the Associate Director in printing student research posters and related tasks. Candidates should be friendly, open-minded, and technologically inquisitive. Good communication skills and customer service orientation are a must. Read more Dean, College of Liberal Arts, Social and Behavioral Sciences, Education, Mathematics and Computer Sciences- A00741 492663 New York, United States Provost's Office Faculty Management Staff Faculty Full-time Staff Full-time Mercy University invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of a newly established College (name to be determined) that brings together the liberal arts, social and behavioral sciences, education, mathematics, and computer sciences in a unified academic home dedicated to interdisciplinary learning, academic excellence, student success, and preparation for a rapidly changing workforce. This is an exciting time to be at Mercy University, as the Dean will have the unique opportunity to shape the future of this transformative entity from its inception. Read more Clinical Educator - Speech and Hearing Center -TA4110 492659 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Health & Natural Sciences Staff Staff Part-Time The Speech and Hearing Center at Mercy University, Dobbs Ferry Campus is seeking a Part-time Clinical Educator to supervise graduate student clinicians. Preferred specialty in childhood apraxia of speech and/or speech sound disorders. Read more Assistant Director, UG Admissions- A00393 492654 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Admissions Staff Staff Full-time Mercy College seeks an Assistant Director of Recruitment. This is a highly visible position responsible for increasing awareness and building enthusiasm for Mercy College through student recruitment initiatives, outreach and communication, and specialized events. The Assistant Director develops partnerships with high schools, counselors, and local college preparatory organizations as well as manages a team of recruiters responsible for freshmen admissions. The Assistant Director oversees the daily operations of the Dobbs Ferry campus freshmen team including the recruitment calendar, campus tours, schedules, etc. The Assistant Director generates inquiries from prospective students that convert to enrolled students. 70% on road recruitment activities. While generating interest and excitement for the Mercy College experience, this position will focus on recruitment efforts for the territories that the Dobbs Ferry recruitment team are responsible for. Read more PACT Mentor, Graduate PACT -P00220 492653 Bronx, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Staff Staff Full-time The PACT Mentor of the Professional Advising and Coaching Team (PACT) plays a vital role in supporting University Advisement initiatives aligned with the University's Strategic Plan. This role reinforces the advising mission and commitment to offer structured advising, actionable mentorship, proactive intervention, and a demonstrated standard of care to all Mercy students. This position combines academic advising, career exploration, and holistic student support to ensure every student feels welcomed, supported, and empowered to succeed and graduate on time. Read more Business Analyst -A00735 492650 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Information Technology Information Technology Staff Staff Full-time The Business Analyst serves as a key member of the Office of Information Technology and is responsible for partnering with stakeholders across the University to identify business needs, gather and document requirements, develop functional specifications, and support the successful delivery of technology and process improvement initiatives. Read more Director of Advancement Operations- A00279 492417 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Institutional Advancement Staff Staff Full-time The Director of Advancement Operations is responsible for providing strategic vision and day-to-day oversight of all advancement services, including gift processing, database management, prospect research, reporting and analytics, and operational policy development. The successful candidate will embrace data-driven decision-making, foster collaborative relationships, and model the highest standards of integrity and professionalism. Read more Dean, College of Business & Entrepreneurship and Communication and the Arts - A00740 492664 New York, United States Provost's Office Faculty Management Staff Faculty Full-time Staff Full-time Mercy University invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of a newly established College (name to be determined) that brings together business, entrepreneurship, communication, digital media, design, and the performing arts in a unified academic home dedicated to innovation, creative enterprise, professional preparation, student success, and preparation for a rapidly changing economic, digital, and creative workforce. This is an exciting time to be at Mercy University, as the Dean will have the unique opportunity to shape the future of this transformative entity from its inception. Read more Men's Lacrosse Coaches- ML3727 492512 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Staff Part-Time Mercy University seeks a passionate and experienced Staff Part-Time Men's Lacrosse Coach to join our Admissions & Recruitment team. This unique position combines coaching excellence with student recruitment, offering an opportunity to shape both athletic and academic success for prospective student-athletes. Read more Field Hockey Coaches- FH3710 492381 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University is looking for Field Hockey Coaches! Read more Student Services Support Center Counselor- P00072 492703 Remote Student Services Support Center Staff Staff Full-time Under the direction of the Assistant Director of Student Services Support Center, the Counselor will assist in the processing of the daily activities and projects of the Student Services Support Center. SSSC will collaborate with Admissions, Recruiting, Business Operations, PACT, and Enrollment Services to ensure professional, efficient and compliant counseling of students. Along with the processing of student records, counselors will be conducting outreach calls and fielding incoming telephone calls, emails, and messages, responding to inquiries for potential, current and former students. The Counselor will further support the activities of the Assistant Director/Associate Director by assisting in training team members. Read more Simulation Lab Assistant - Dobbs Ferry- LB4121 492699 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Nursing Staff Staff Part-Time The Simulation Lab Assistant provides crucial operational, technical, and administrative support to\nthe Simulation Center and the Director of Simulation. This role ensures the smooth daily operation\nof the nursing simulation labs, prepares high-fidelity and low-fidelity environments for student\nexperiences, manages specialized inventory, and assists faculty and students during active\nsimulation scenarios, skill labs, and objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs). Read more Simulation Lab Assistant - Bronx-  LB4120 492671 Bronx, New York, United States School of Nursing Staff Staff Part-Time The Simulation Lab Assistant provides crucial operational, technical, and administrative support to the Simulation Center and the Director of Simulation. This role ensures the smooth daily operation of the nursing simulation labs, prepares high-fidelity and low-fidelity environments for student experiences, manages specialized inventory, and assists faculty and students during active simulation scenarios, skill labs, and objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs). Read more Director of Advancement Performance- A00403 492696 Tarrytown, New York, United States Institutional Advancement Staff Staff Full-time The Director of Advancement Performance is a strategic, hands-on advancement professional responsible for managing a portfolio of major and leadership gift prospects while overseeing the execution of core fundraising programs. This role bridges frontline fundraising, annual giving, and general development outreach to drive philanthropic results and ensure efficient, data-informed advancement practices. Read more Assistant Volleyball Coach- VB3735 492672 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University's Athletics program is looking for a dedicated Assistant Volleyball Coach to join its competitive NCAA Division II program at the Dobbs Ferry campus. If you bring hands-on coaching experience and a genuine commitment to student-athlete development, this is a meaningful opportunity to contribute to a program that takes both athletic performance and academic success seriously. Read more Manager of Employer Relations- A00738 492662 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Staff Staff Full-time The Manager of Employer Relations plays a vital role in supporting the employer engagement strategy at Mercy University. Working under the direction of the Director of Employer Relations, the manager maintains assigned employer relationships and supports the development of new partnerships with corporate, regional, and local private and public sector employers. The manager plans and executes employer events in addition to gathering and promoting experiential learning opportunities for Mercy University students across all schools. This position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to build and maintain professional relationships. The manager is expected to perform other duties as assigned; occasional weekend and evening hours may be required. Read more Career Counselor- P00256 492661 Bronx, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Staff Staff Full-time The Career Counselor is a key player in implementing a comprehensive suite of career readiness programs, tools, resources, and services for Mercy College. The Career Counselor offers career coaching to students, hosts and supports programming, conducts proactive outreach to students, and offers career support through classroom visits. In addition, the Career Counselor supports one or two major projects for the team; major projects in Career & Professional Development include career in curriculum, data management, technology systems, and marketing. Read more Associate Director, University Advisement- A00207 492668 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Staff Staff Full-time The Associate Director of University Advisement is responsible for being highly accessible, integrating services and programs in academic advising, student intervention and support, professional integrations for student development, academic integrations for student development, and social integration for student development. The Associate Director supervises a team of staff that will also provide these services in a detailed and tailored approach, positing mentorship as a key relationship dynamic and providing an intentional standard of care. These services and programs will support student success, self-efficacy, and a transformational college experience, maximizing the student-centered approach and deepening connection to the Mercy University community through all years of enrollment matriculation. Read more Associate Director, Career Education- A00205 492666 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Staff Staff Full-time The Associate Director provides leadership and advanced support in the design, delivery, assessment, and continuous improvement of career education, programming, and technology tools that advance student career readiness across Mercy University locations and online. This role collaborates closely with the Career & Professional Development team and campus partners to develop high-impact career education initiatives, provide career coaching to students and alumni, lead proactive student engagement strategies, and support career education through classroom visits, workshops, events, and targeted communications. The Associate Director also plays a leadership role in managing and optimizing the department’s technology ecosystem by overseeing select platforms, maintaining documentation, partnering with vendors and IT on implementation and troubleshooting, and using data to improve student engagement and career outcomes. As a member of the broader Experiential Education and Career Development team, this position contributes to departmental strategy, cross-campus operations, assessment efforts, staff support, and project leadership that enhance student engagement, career readiness, experiential learning, and post-graduation outcomes. Read more PACT Mentor- P00152 492660 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Staff Staff Full-time The PACT Mentor of the Professional Advising and Coaching Team (PACT) plays a vital role in supporting University Advisement initiatives aligned with the University's Strategic Plan. This role reinforces the advising mission and commitment to offer structured advising, actionable mentorship, proactive intervention, and a demonstrated standard of care to all Mercy students. This position combines academic advising, career exploration, and holistic student support to ensure every student feels welcomed, supported, and empowered to succeed and graduate on time. Read more Assistant Director, PACT 492651 Bronx, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Staff Staff Full-time The Assistant Director of the Professional Advising and Coaching Team (P.A.C.T.) plays a vital role in supporting University Advisement initiatives aligned with the University's Strategic Plan. The assistant director role reinforces the advising mission and commitment to offer structured advising, actionable mentorship, proactive intervention, and a demonstrated standard of care to all Mercy students. This position collaborates with the Associate Director of University Advisement to ensure the effective delivery of services and resources to a diverse student population. Read more Associate Director, Admissions (A00695) 492583 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Admissions Staff Staff Full-time The Associate Director of Admissions Dobbs Ferry Campus plays a critical leadership role in the strategic planning, development, and execution of recruitment and admissions initiatives. This position supports the Director of Admissions in meeting enrollment goals by managing staff, developing outreach strategies, evaluating applications, and enhancing the admissions process. The Associate Director serves as a key representative of the institution, fostering relationships with prospective students, families, schools, and community organizations. The Associate Director will recruit in Westchester County and supervises the Assistant Directors on our Dobbs Ferry Campus. Read more Special Projects - Math CS Proctor 492646 New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Staff Staff Part-Time Join Mercy University as a Staff Part-Time Proctor for the MATH & CS Department, where you’ll play\nan essential role in supporting students to achieve their academic goals. This role specifically supports\nand proctors online class modalities for in-person exams. This position offers flexible scheduling and the\nchance to make a meaningful impact on student success. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 51 in total ‹ 1 2 › Equal Opportunity Consistent with its obligations under the law, Mercy University will provide reasonable accommodation to any employee with a disability who requires accommodation to perform the essential functions of the job. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Categories Accounting Careers Technology Careers Education Careers Administration Careers Recruiting Careers Quick Links About Us Contact Us Contribute Privacy Policy Sitemap © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Mercy University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its funct