nd the Arts Department at Mercy University seeks part-time, adjunct instructors to teach general education courses to undergraduate students. Read more Adjunct Faculty MTECH 492621 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Adjunct Faculty Part Time The Music Production & Record Arts Program in the Communications & The Arts Department of the School of Liberal Arts at Mercy University seeks a passionate, dedicated, and experienced Music Production instructor. This position offers opportunities to teach Electronic Music Production I, Electronic Music Production II, Synthesis, Electronic Music Performance, Game Music, and MAX/MSP, as well as other courses commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications in those areas, up to a maximum of three sections per semester. Read more Assistant Professor and Clinical Director, Counseling (F00268) 492599 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Social & Behavorial Sci Faculty Faculty Full-time The School of Social and Behavioral Sciences at Mercy University invites applications for a full-time, multi-year Assistant Professor/Clinical Director of Counseling position in the Department of Counseling, overseeing field experience for the School Counseling and Mental Health Counseling programs. This is an exciting opportunity to join a dedicated and engaged team as the Department of Counseling prepares CACREP accreditation to further strengthen its graduate programs and student outcomes. The Clinical Director role includes an additional stipend and a course release to support administrative and programmatic responsibilities associated with field experience coordination. This position requires regular on-campus presence. Limited flexibility for remote work may be available in alignment with departmental needs and responsibilities. Read more Adjunct Faculty- Vet Tech 492329 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Health & Natural Sciences Adjunct Faculty Part Time The Veterinary Technology Program is seeking adjunct faculty for the upcoming academic term with a special interest in teaching pharmacology.  Additional co-teaching responsibilities may also include clinical laboratories.  An adjunct faculty member is directly responsible and accountable for fulfillment of Program learning outcomes as well as ensuring compliance with the AVMA-CVTEA accreditation standards.  Appointments are renewed based on Program needs and teaching performance. Read more Adjunct Faculty- Mathematics 492345 New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Adjunct Faculty Part Time The Department of Mathematics and Computer Sciences at Mercy University (NY) invites applicants for adjunct faculty positions in Mathematics to begin January 2025. Read more Adjunct Faculty Humanities (AF2205) 492565 New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Adjunct Faculty Part Time The First-Year Seminar Program at Mercy University seeks part-time adjunct instructors to teach first-year seminars to incoming freshmen. The First-Year Seminar is designed to acclimate students to college life. Instructors support students in navigating their first semester by teaching essential skills for a successful college career, introducing university resources, and encouraging students to think about their career pathways. Read more Adjunct Faculty English 492346 Bronx, New York, United States Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Manhattan, New York, United States New York, United States Show More Show Less School of Liberal Arts Adjunct Faculty Part Time The English Program at Mercy University seeks part-time adjunct instructors to teach English composition to undergraduate students. Commitment to inclusive, student-centered teaching is required. Candidates may also be asked to provide assistance with program assessment and to attend select programmatic or professional development meetings. Successful candidates may be offered the opportunity to teach up to 3 section(s) per semester. Read more Adjunct Facu