      "description": "Search Page About Mercy Why Mercy (current) Mercy in the News View All Jobs My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode With Every Opportunity the World Transforms Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 10 filter options found Category Adjunct (0 items) 0 Admissions (0 items) 0 Athletics/Coaching (0 items) 0 Campus Employment (34 items) 34 Faculty (0 items) 0 Higher Education (1 items) 1 Information Technology (0 items) 0 Library (1 items) 1 Management (0 items) 0 Staff (0 items) 0 Department Search departments 21 filter options found Department Admissions & Recruitment (0 items) 0 Athletics (0 items) 0 Center for Student Success (3 items) 3 Faculty Development (2 items) 2 Grants (6 items) 6 Information Technology (0 items) 0 Institutional Advancement (0 items) 0 Libraries, Inst Tech & Online Learn (1 items) 1 Marketing & Communication (0 items) 0 Office of Student Financial Service (0 items) 0 Operations and Facilities (0 items) 0 Provost's Office (8 items) 8 School of Business (1 items) 1 School of Education (1 items) 1 School of Health & Natural Sciences (5 items) 5 School of Liberal Arts (4 items) 4 School of Nursing (0 items) 0 School of Social & Behavorial Sci (0 items) 0 Student Clubs Assoc Activities (1 items) 1 Student Services Support Center (0 items) 0 Student Srvs Auxiliary (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 5 filter options found Employment Type Faculty Full-time (0 items) 0 Faculty Part Time (0 items) 0 Staff Full-time (0 items) 0 Staff Part-Time (0 items) 0 Student worker (34 items) 34 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Student Worker SLA MIT (TIER1) 492700 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Campus Employment Student worker These administrative positions may include all or some of the following duties: copying, filing, answering telephones, greeting visitors, data entry, creating documents, assisting with event planning, liasing with students, faculty and staff, creating flyers and forms, attending events, etc. These are entry-level jobs that do not require specialized skills or training and will require specific instructions and oversight. Read more Graduate Residential Coordinator (Tier 3) 492701 Manhattan, New York, United States Student Srvs Auxiliary Campus Employment Student worker This is a unique role for a current graduate student that provides the opportunity to enhance leadership, interpersonal, networking and communication skills in the Office of Residential Life. The Residential Coordinator will work closely with the professional staff to create and contribute to the enhancement of an on-campus living and learning environment conducive to student success.\nReporting to the Associate Director of Residential Life (AD), the Residential Coordinator is a part-time live-in position at Dorm34 under a 10-month contract from August 2026 to May 2027. Read more Student Worker - Peer Tutor 492348 New York, United States Center for Student Success Campus Employment Student worker This position provides for tutoring and academic support to fellow students. In their interactions, they model good student practices such as study and note-taking strategies, help their peers develop time management skills, and foster confidence and self-reliance. May conduct and lead group study and tutoring sessions in a variety of formats, such as Supplemental Instruction (SI) and Structured Learning Assistance (SLA). In this role, they encourage student success through engagement with a variety of academic resources. Read more Student Worker – Office of the Provost (TIER1) 492697 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker The Academic Affairs Assistant positions will support various programs and departments within Academic Affairs. The role will offer general administrative support to the Academic departments and the Libraries. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with a wonderful opportunity to learn about Mercy University and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\nThis role will require general office software application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player.\nThese positions will vary between 12-15 hours a week, will pay NYS minimum wage, and will be in effect for the 2026-27 Academic Year. Read more Student Worker Mentee (Undergraduate) 492694 New York, United States Libraries, Inst Tech & Online Learn Campus Employment Library Student worker Library Student Mentees will perform the following duties:\n\nServe as the Library’s first point of contact, welcoming and assisting students, faculty, and staff with a consistently professional, service-oriented demeanor.\nCurate and sustain shelf integrity by organizing, shelving, and maintaining the cleanliness and navigability of assigned collections to established standards.\nExecute all front-desk/circulation transactions with precision and compliance to standard operating procedures, ensuring data accuracy and patron confidentiality.\nTriage, answer, and appropriately route inbound telephone inquiries; document messages and escalate issues per communication protocols.\nOperate multifunction devices to produce copies, scans, and faxes; verify output quality and resolve routine user issues.\nMonitor and replenish consumables (e.g., printer and copier paper) to maintain continuous service availability; log inventory changes as directed.\nProvide Tier-1 technical assistance for patrons (e.g., printing, scanning, account access), including basic troubleshooting and timely escalation.\nConsistently demonstrate reliability, sound judgment, and a positive, professional presence; model customer-service best practices under varying demand levels.\nMaintain a safe, orderly, and audit-ready circulation and office environment by cleaning, organizing, and restocking supplies throughout the shift.\nFulfill Interlibrary Loan (ILL) requests by locating materials, verifying bibliographic details, and assisting with packaging, labeling, and processing to meet shipment timelines.\n \n\nIn addition to circulation:\n\nEngage in structured, mentor-guided exploration of academic and career pathways; establish goals and reflect on progress through scheduled check-ins.\nTranslate on-the-job responsibilities into resume-ready competencies by collaborating with the mentor and librarians to identify transferable skills and career applications.\nComplete curated microlearning (videos, articles, activities) aligned to career development milestones; document takeaways and action steps.\nPartner with Career Services for tailored resume refinement and interview preparation, integrating feedback into a professional portfolio.\nAuthor a librarian-supported research guide on a self-selected topic, demonstrating information literacy, audience awareness, and effective resource curation. Read more Graduate Residential Coordinator (Tier 3) 492695 Manhattan, New York, United States Student Srvs Auxiliary Campus Employment Student worker This is a unique role for a current graduate student that provides the opportunity to enhance leadership, interpersonal,\nnetworking and communication skills in the Office of Residential Life. The Residential Coordinator will work closely with the\nprofessional staff to create and contribute to the enhancement of an on-campus living and learning environment conducive\nto student success.\nReporting to the Associate Director of Residential Life (AD), the Residential Coordinator is a part-time live-in position at\nDorm34 under a 10-month contract from August 2026 to May 2027.\nResponsibilities include:\nStaff supervision\nAssist the AD with the supervision and training of Resident Assistants (RAs) in the areas of programming, crisis\nresponse, collaboration, and campus culture\nParticipate in RA training in the winter and summer as well as supplemental in-services and professional development\nopportunities\nOversee Desk Attendants (DAs) and RAs in the absence of professional staff members\nStudent Development and Engagement\nProvide leadership and support to the residential community at Dorm34\nRegularly interact with students and provide availability both during the day and in the evening hours\nAct in an advising capacity and refer students to appropriate campus offices, services, and resources in accordance\nwith the Student Handbook and Residential Life policies\nFollow up with student concerns, act as a liaison to ensure timeliness of reporting and service completion\nAssist with health and safety inspections and roommate mediations\nCrisis Response\nServe in the duty in collaboration with other live in staff at Manhattan campus (approximately two weeks per month)\nRespond to incidents in a timely manner and report them in accordance with policy\nAttend staff trainings to adequately and appropriately respond to incidents\nOther\nAttend various meetings with campus stakeholders\nAssist with administrative processes, policies, and procedures\nAbility to travel between campuses Read more Student Worker NYS HEOP (TIER1) 492657 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Grants Campus Employment Student worker Participate in ongoing training sessions conducted by the Project Director and Assistant Director prior to the beginning of the summer program or academic year\nAttend classes and eat lunch with HEOP students to develop trust and rapport\nServe as role models for HEOP students\nProvide one-on-one or small group tutoring to students\nAssist the summer program faculty in the classroom\nMeet with faculty and HEOP professional counselors to discuss academic problems that individual students may have\nParticipate in select HEOP staff meetings\nProvide written reports of student progress and submit these to the Associate Director Read more Student Worker – BX Nursing PF (TIER1) 492458 Bronx, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker Academic Affairs Assistant\n\nThe Academic Affairs Assistant positions will support various programs and departments within Academic Affairs. The role will offer general administrative support to the Academic departments and the libraries. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with a wonderful opportunity to learn about Mercy University and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\n\nThis role will require general office application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player.\n\nThese positions will vary between 12-15 hours a week, will pay $16.50 per hour, and will be in effect for the 2025-26 Academic Year. Read more Student Worker TV DHSI CG (TIER2) 492364 New York, United States Grants Campus Employment Student worker Student Affairs is looking to hire a new group of Mercy Navigators! Read more Student Worker PT (TIER1) - CE0044 492615 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Health & Natural Sciences Campus Employment Student worker Mercy University is seeking candidates for a part-time, graduate student worker level-1. The Graduate Student worker (level 1) will be responsible for general administrative duties including copying, filing, answering the phone/emails, creating documents, equipment set-up, assisting with event planning and working closely with faculty, current and prospective students and the program administrative assistant. The student worker -L1 should be willing and able to participate in training in specific database systems used by the program including but not limited to Physical Therapy Centralized Application System (PTCAS) and Clinic documentation and scheduling systems. Read more Student Worker SB SL Academy (TIER1) 492626 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Business Campus Employment Student worker Responsibilities include, but are not limited to:\n\nMeet daily at 9:00 a.m. with the School of Business Director of Business Operations to review the day’s agenda and activities.\nEnsure that Summer Leadership Academy participants have their materials, including booklets, pens, and appropriate attire for scheduled activities.\nHelp ensure participants arrive to and depart from meals on time in order to maintain the program’s schedule.\nAssist with evening sports, games, and team-building activities on Mercy University’s campus, including events such as Game Night, Karaoke Night, and Movie Night.\nHelp ensure participant safety and adherence to program expectations, including being indoors by 8:00 p.m., returning to the residence hall by 11:00 p.m., and observing lights out at 12:00 a.m. to support adequate rest for the following day’s activities.\nCollect photos and materials for the Summer Leadership Academy graduation slideshow.\nPerform other related duties as assigned by the School of Business. Read more Student Worker CD (TIER 3) 492617 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Faculty Development Campus Employment Student worker Students who have been chosen by Faculty Development Grant recipients as Research Assistants should apply for this position in order to facilitate their payment. You should only apply for this position if you have explicitly been told to do so by faculty. Read more Student Worker Summer Position 492291 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Student Clubs Assoc Activities Campus Employment Higher Education Student worker Fitness Center position: Reporting to the Head Strength & Conditioning Coach and Assistant Strength & Conditioning Coach, the Fitness Center Student Worker is responsible for assisting in supervision of all aspects of the Hudson Hall Fitness Center. Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Managing student and staff check in process during open hours, attending to daily gym maintenance; upkeep and cleanliness of the fitness center; overseeing fitness center use; enforcing policies and procedures; tracking and reporting ongoing patron usage statistics; providing positive energy and friendly service to student and staff population during use of the fitness center. This position will require varied hours. Read more Lab Assistant – Student Worker PA (CE4533) 492581 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Health & Natural Sciences Campus Employment Student worker A lab assistant for the PA Program’s anatomy lab is highly specialized, often bridging the gap between faculty and a large class of up to 70 students. The role blends deep anatomical knowledge with teaching, professionalism, and lab-specific technical skills. They have advanced training and expertise on the Anatomage table, and advanced knowledge of anatomy, particularly as seen on a digital platform. This specialized skill set is essential for performing the role of lab assistant in a virtual anatomy lab. Read more SAGE Student Worker (TIER 3) 492572 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Campus Employment Student worker Looking for Teaching Assistants for the Mathematical Modeling at Mercy University (M3U) summer program at the Dobbs Ferry campus. The job runs from 7/6 - 8/1, Monday-Friday 10:15am-4:15pm, plus a Saturday banquet on 8/1. TAs will help high school students with math problems, explain math concepts, guide a team of five students on an applied math project, grade problem sets, and otherwise help out with the activities of the M3U summer program. Read more Specl. Proj. MATH TA 492537 New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Campus Employment Student worker This position provides for in-class tutoring and academic support for fellow students. They work closely with the course instructor, assisting with classroom activities. In their interactions, Math Teaching Assistants (TAs) model good student practices such as study and note-taking strategies, help their peers develop time management skills, and foster confidence and self-reliance. They encourage student success through engagement with a variety of academic resources. \nPosition Requirements: \n•\tMust demonstrate an ability to quickly establish rapport and communicate well with students and instructors. \n•\tMust demonstrate mastery of the specific content area or a related subject area in which he or she will assist students in the classroom. \n•\tMust provide name of one Mercy College faculty member who will provide a letter of support on their behalf.  \n•\tMust maintain an overall GPA of 3.0 and an average of B+ or better in subjects in which they will assist students in the classroom.  \nDuties and responsibilities: \n•\tAttend required classes on time and be prepared. \n•\tCommunicate, collaborate and assist the course instructor with classroom activities. \n•\tAssist students, individuals or small groups, to understand topic concepts, methods, and classroom assignments. \n•\tAssist students to understand the syllabus, class assignments, and how to input answers in Blackboard. \n•\tComply with policies and procedures of the Department and the College including but not limited to the College’s Code of Conduct and maintain students’ information confidentiality. \n•\tAccurately log work hours on Banner timesheets in Mercy Connect and submit them on time. \n•\tAttend training and professional development workshops. • Meet with CAEI Supervisor. \nTeaching Assistants Do Not: \n•\tAssist students solving Tests and/or Quizzes, write or edit students’ writing assignments. \n•\tUse cell phones, their laptops, tablets and/or any other personal electronic device in class. \n•\tPerform tasks unrelated to the position such as doing their own homework, assignments, or any other unrelated activity during class. \n•\tBring food and eat in class. Read more Student Worker – School of Business (TIER1) 492464 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker The Academic Affairs Assistant positions will support various programs and departments within Academic Affairs. The role will offer general administrative support to the Academic departments and the Libraries. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with an opportunity to learn about Mercy University and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\n\n\nThis role will require general office software application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player. Read more Student Worker Catalyst Program PF (TIER1) 492463 Bronx, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker The student worker position will support the Catalyst Program in the Bronx. The role will offer general administrative support, including helping students navigate their eBooks on the Barnes & Noble system and work with the bookstore. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with an opportunity to learn about Mercy University and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\n\nThis role will require general office software application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player.\n\nThese positions will vary between 12-15 hours a week, will pay $16.50 per hour, and will be in effect for the 2025-26 Academic Year. Read more Student Worker SLA RL (TIER2) 492392 New York, United States Center for Student Success Campus Employment Student worker The goal of the Supplemental Instruction (SI) program is to support student success through structured opportunities for interactive group learning led by Learning Fellows, near-peers who can model success strategies. SI activities support both content learning as well as improvement of study skills and development of community. SI provides students with additional time outside of the traditional class to process material and practice skills in a low-pressure environment. In addition, it supports the development of an inclusive community of collaborative learners. Read more Student Worker CD (TIER 3) 492564 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Faculty Development Campus Employment Student worker Students who have been chosen by Faculty Development Grant recipients as Research Assistants should apply for this position in order to facilitate their payment Read more Student Worker VT (TIER1) 492411 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Health & Natural Sciences Campus Employment Student worker The Veterinary Technology Department, School of Health and Natural Sciences, is seeking student workers for the upcoming semester. The role will offer general support to the Veterinary Technology Program, including instructional support and office duties. Read more Student Worker USDOE SR (Tier 2) 492296 New York, United States Grants Campus Employment Student worker -Students hired into peer mentor roles will assist student research participants and research faculty in the STEM Ready Summer Research Institute. Duties include assisting with literature searches, lab set-up, assistance with protocols, lab preparation and assisting students with experiments, data analyses, technical projects and research presentations.\n\n-Internship students carry out duties related to their off-site internships. Specific duties are set by the internship site. Read more Student Worker PA PF (TIER1) 492505 Bronx, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker Provides essential administrative and admissions support to the Mercy University PA Program by assisting with applicant communications, file organization, interview preparation, and daily operational tasks. Read more Junior Programs Facilitator 492499 Tarrytown, New York, United States School of Education Campus Employment Student worker Junior Programs Facilitator supports the Assistant Director with the Saturday STEM Academy, the Verizon Innovative Learning STEM Summer Program, and other Center for STEM Education events. Read more Student Worker – ARMRF Research Grant (TIER2) 492484 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Grants Campus Employment Student worker The SHNS is seeking graduate students to work as research assistants on the Age-Related Movement: Live Stronger, Move Better Rainwater Foundation Grant.  The role will be to assist the principal investigators with recruitment, data collection, and participant follow-up. Read more Student Worker – ARMRF Research Grant (TIER3) 492485 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Grants Campus Employment Student worker The SHNS is looking for a graduate student to work as student research assistant on the Age-Related Movement: Live Stronger, Move Better Rainwater Foundation Grant.  This position will serve as the Project Manager. They will assist the PIs with scheduling all participants and work with the data dashboard to ensure data is collected accurately as well as the above. This role will also assist the principal investigators with recruitment, data collection, and participant follow-up. Read more Student Worker CS (TIER3) 492482 New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Campus Employment Student worker The teaching assistant assists the instructor in their classroom as well as outside the classroom. Duties include grading of homework, helping students with any questions they may have with concepts and/or skills in the course, and tutoring students as needed. Read more Student Worker – DF Nursing PF (TIER1) 492457 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker The Student Worker posting in Dobbs Ferry will support various programs and departments within the Nursing School. The role will offer general administrative support to the simulation and operations departments. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with an opportunity to learn about Mercy University and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\n\nThis role will require general office software application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player.\n\nThese positions will vary between 12-15 hours a week, will pay $16.50 per hour, and will be in effect for the 2025-26 Academic Year. Read more Student Worker – CommDis PF (TIER1) 492453 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker The Academic Affairs Assistant positions will support various programs and departments within Academic Affairs. The role will offer general administrative support to the Academic departments and the Libraries. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with an opportunity to learn about Mercy College and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\n\nThis role will require general office software application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player.\n\nThese positions will vary between 12-15 hours a week. Read more Student Worker PO (TIER1) 492443 New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker The Academic Affairs Assistant positions will support various programs and departments within Academic Affairs. The role will offer general administrative support to the Academic departments and the Libraries. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with a wonderful opportunity to learn about Mercy College and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\n\nThis role will require general office software application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player.\n\nThese positions will vary between 12-15 hours a week, will pay $16.50 per hour, and will be in effect for the 2025-26 Academic Year. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 34 in total ‹ 1 2 › Equal Opportunity Consistent with its obligations under the law, Mercy University will provide reasonable accommodation to any employee with a disability who requires accommodation to perform the essential functions of the job. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Categories Accounting Careers Technology Careers Education Careers Administration Careers Recruiting Careers Quick Links About Us Contact Us Contribute Privacy Policy Sitemap © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Mercy University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
