      "description": "Search Page About Mercy Why Mercy (current) Mercy in the News View All Jobs My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode With Every Opportunity the World Transforms Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 10 filter options found Category Adjunct (28 items) 28 Admissions (5 items) 5 Athletics/Coaching (10 items) 10 Campus Employment (34 items) 34 Faculty (4 items) 4 Higher Education (1 items) 1 Information Technology (2 items) 2 Library (3 items) 3 Management (2 items) 2 Staff (43 items) 43 Department Search departments 21 filter options found Department Admissions & Recruitment (14 items) 14 Athletics (9 items) 9 Center for Student Success (4 items) 4 Faculty Development (2 items) 2 Grants (6 items) 6 Information Technology (2 items) 2 Institutional Advancement (4 items) 4 Libraries, Inst Tech & Online Learn (3 items) 3 Marketing & Communication (1 items) 1 Office of Student Financial Service (1 items) 1 Operations and Facilities (2 items) 2 Provost's Office (12 items) 12 School of Business (6 items) 6 School of Education (5 items) 5 School of Health & Natural Sciences (18 items) 18 School of Liberal Arts (14 items) 14 School of Nursing (5 items) 5 School of Social & Behavorial Sci (2 items) 2 Student Clubs Assoc Activities (1 items) 1 Student Services Support Center (1 items) 1 Student Srvs Auxiliary (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 5 filter options found Employment Type Faculty Full-time (5 items) 5 Faculty Part Time (28 items) 28 Staff Full-time (32 items) 32 Staff Part-Time (19 items) 19 Student worker (34 items) 34 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Baseball Coach- BB3720 492707 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University's baseball program is looking for a dedicated Assistant Baseball Coach to join its Athletics staff at the Dobbs Ferry campus. If you're ready to invest in student-athletes both on the field and in the classroom, this is a role where your coaching expertise genuinely shapes lives. Read more Learning Support Manager- A00744 492709 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Staff Staff Full-time The Learning Support Manager for the Center for Academic Excellence and Innovation (CAEI) provides coordination and oversight of academic support services designed to enhance student learning, persistence, and academic success. Reporting to the CAEI Director, the Learning Support Manager is responsible for managing tutoring operations, developing and supporting peer tutors, faculty tutors, and strengthening partnerships with faculty, academic departments, and student success teams.\nThe Learning Support Manager serves as a campus leader for academic support by ensuring students have access to high-quality, proactive, and inclusive learning resources. This position supports CAEI’s mission to promote independent learning, increase utilization of tutoring services, improve student outcomes in high-need courses, contributing to institutional retention and on-time graduation. Read more Assistant Director of Student Financial Services- A00217 492710 Manhattan, New York, United States Office of Student Financial Service Staff Staff Full-time Under the direction of the Senior Assistant Director of Student Financial Services, the Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will assist in the management of the daily operations of the Student Financial Services Offices to support the Campus Operations ensuring the professional, efficient and compliant processing of student records.  The Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will assist in the management of the supervision of registration processes, resulting billing processes, and counseling of students and families.  The Assistant Director of Student Financial Services will also serve as a primary supervisor of the Student Financial Services Counselors, ensuring student centered service in meeting the needs of traditional, non-traditional, adult and minority student populations. Read more Women's Flag Football Assistant Coach- WF3700 492711 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University Athletics is building something real on the flag football field, and the right assistant coach will be part of it from the ground up. If you know the game, connect with student-athletes, and want to contribute to a program that competes with purpose, this is your opportunity. Read more Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions- A00307 492685 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Admissions Staff Staff Full-time The Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions supports the Associate Director and Director of Graduate Admissions in achieving enrollment goals across Mercy’s graduate programs. This role focuses on implementing recruitment and admissions initiatives, supervising staff, managing a defined recruitment territory, and cultivating relationships with prospective students, community partners, and academic departments. The Assistant Director contributes to process improvements, supports yield and communication efforts, and represents Mercy at events to expand graduate enrollment and strengthen partnerships. Read more Visiting Assistant Professor- F00330 492706 Manhattan, New York, United States School of Business Faculty Faculty Full-time Mercy University invites applications for a full-time, visiting, non-tenure-track faculty position in Management/Business Administration within the School of Business. The successful candidate will serve in a dual role as Visiting Assistant Professor of Management and Interim Associate Dean for 2026–2027. The Interim Associate Dean assignment is a twelve-month administrative appointment. The faculty role carries a standard 4/4 teaching load, with course release and a stipend provided in recognition of the additional administrative responsibilities. Read more Adjunct Faculty Business 492333 New York, United States School of Business Adjunct Faculty Part Time The School of Business at Mercy University invites applicants for adjunct faculty positions to teach undergraduate and/or graduate Business classes. We seek candidates who demonstrate a commitment to student-centered teaching and can support students from diverse backgrounds. Read more Executive Director, Academic Success and Accessibility (A00736) 492652 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Staff Faculty Full-time Staff Full-time The Executive Director for Academic Success and Accessibility serves as a senior academic leader responsible for advancing an integrated, student-centered model of academic support and accessibility services across Mercy. Reporting to the Senior Vice Provost for Academic Affairs, the Executive Director provides strategic leadership for accessibility services, tutoring, learning support initiatives, early alert interventions, and student success programs designed to improve retention, persistence, academic achievement, and degree completion. Read more Associate Director, Corporate & Foundation Relations- A00743 492704 Tarrytown, New York, United States Institutional Advancement Staff Staff Full-time The Assistant/Associate Director, Corporate & Foundation Relations will support the goals of the Executive Director for Corporate & Foundation Relations (ED CFR) in support of institutional priorities through prospect research and development of letters of interest, proposals, and grant applications. The position will assist in growing the donor population through discovery, qualification and solicitation. The position assists in the management of donor stewardship and engagement which includes preparing door impact reports, and pre- and post-award contract compliance. Read more Library Assistant- C00044 492667 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Libraries, Inst Tech & Online Learn Library Staff Full-time Mercy University Libraries’ is seeking self-motivated, energetic, and detail-oriented candidates to fill a patron centered support role within the Dobbs Ferry Campus Circulation team. Reporting to the Associate Director, the position’s primary duties will include supervising library circulation and reserve operations, assisting students and faculty with library resources and related technology needs. The Library Assistant will collaborate with branch circulation supervisors, the systems librarian, and reference librarians. Additionally, the position will monitor front desk inquiries, library computers, printers, and software resources and support the Associate Director in printing student research posters and related tasks. Candidates should be friendly, open-minded, and technologically inquisitive. Good communication skills and customer service orientation are a must. Read more Dean, College of Liberal Arts, Social and Behavioral Sciences, Education, Mathematics and Computer Sciences- A00741 492663 New York, United States Provost's Office Faculty Management Staff Faculty Full-time Staff Full-time Mercy University invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of a newly established College (name to be determined) that brings together the liberal arts, social and behavioral sciences, education, mathematics, and computer sciences in a unified academic home dedicated to interdisciplinary learning, academic excellence, student success, and preparation for a rapidly changing workforce. This is an exciting time to be at Mercy University, as the Dean will have the unique opportunity to shape the future of this transformative entity from its inception. Read more Clinical Educator - Speech and Hearing Center -TA4110 492659 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Health & Natural Sciences Staff Staff Part-Time The Speech and Hearing Center at Mercy University, Dobbs Ferry Campus is seeking a Part-time Clinical Educator to supervise graduate student clinicians. Preferred specialty in childhood apraxia of speech and/or speech sound disorders. Read more Assistant Director, UG Admissions- A00393 492654 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Admissions Staff Staff Full-time Mercy College seeks an Assistant Director of Recruitment. This is a highly visible position responsible for increasing awareness and building enthusiasm for Mercy College through student recruitment initiatives, outreach and communication, and specialized events. The Assistant Director develops partnerships with high schools, counselors, and local college preparatory organizations as well as manages a team of recruiters responsible for freshmen admissions. The Assistant Director oversees the daily operations of the Dobbs Ferry campus freshmen team including the recruitment calendar, campus tours, schedules, etc. The Assistant Director generates inquiries from prospective students that convert to enrolled students. 70% on road recruitment activities. While generating interest and excitement for the Mercy College experience, this position will focus on recruitment efforts for the territories that the Dobbs Ferry recruitment team are responsible for. Read more PACT Mentor, Graduate PACT -P00220 492653 Bronx, New York, United States Admissions & Recruitment Staff Staff Full-time The PACT Mentor of the Professional Advising and Coaching Team (PACT) plays a vital role in supporting University Advisement initiatives aligned with the University's Strategic Plan. This role reinforces the advising mission and commitment to offer structured advising, actionable mentorship, proactive intervention, and a demonstrated standard of care to all Mercy students. This position combines academic advising, career exploration, and holistic student support to ensure every student feels welcomed, supported, and empowered to succeed and graduate on time. Read more Business Analyst -A00735 492650 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Information Technology Information Technology Staff Staff Full-time The Business Analyst serves as a key member of the Office of Information Technology and is responsible for partnering with stakeholders across the University to identify business needs, gather and document requirements, develop functional specifications, and support the successful delivery of technology and process improvement initiatives. Read more Director of Advancement Operations- A00279 492417 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Institutional Advancement Staff Staff Full-time The Director of Advancement Operations is responsible for providing strategic vision and day-to-day oversight of all advancement services, including gift processing, database management, prospect research, reporting and analytics, and operational policy development. The successful candidate will embrace data-driven decision-making, foster collaborative relationships, and model the highest standards of integrity and professionalism. Read more Dean, College of Business & Entrepreneurship and Communication and the Arts - A00740 492664 New York, United States Provost's Office Faculty Management Staff Faculty Full-time Staff Full-time Mercy University invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of a newly established College (name to be determined) that brings together business, entrepreneurship, communication, digital media, design, and the performing arts in a unified academic home dedicated to innovation, creative enterprise, professional preparation, student success, and preparation for a rapidly changing economic, digital, and creative workforce. This is an exciting time to be at Mercy University, as the Dean will have the unique opportunity to shape the future of this transformative entity from its inception. Read more Men's Lacrosse Coaches- ML3727 492512 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Staff Part-Time Mercy University seeks a passionate and experienced Staff Part-Time Men's Lacrosse Coach to join our Admissions & Recruitment team. This unique position combines coaching excellence with student recruitment, offering an opportunity to shape both athletic and academic success for prospective student-athletes. Read more Field Hockey Coaches- FH3710 492381 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University is looking for Field Hockey Coaches! Read more Student Services Support Center Counselor- P00072 492703 Remote Student Services Support Center Staff Staff Full-time Under the direction of the Assistant Director of Student Services Support Center, the Counselor will assist in the processing of the daily activities and projects of the Student Services Support Center. SSSC will collaborate with Admissions, Recruiting, Business Operations, PACT, and Enrollment Services to ensure professional, efficient and compliant counseling of students. Along with the processing of student records, counselors will be conducting outreach calls and fielding incoming telephone calls, emails, and messages, responding to inquiries for potential, current and former students. The Counselor will further support the activities of the Assistant Director/Associate Director by assisting in training team members. Read more Simulation Lab Assistant - Dobbs Ferry- LB4121 492699 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Nursing Staff Staff Part-Time The Simulation Lab Assistant provides crucial operational, technical, and administrative support to\nthe Simulation Center and the Director of Simulation. This role ensures the smooth daily operation\nof the nursing simulation labs, prepares high-fidelity and low-fidelity environments for student\nexperiences, manages specialized inventory, and assists faculty and students during active\nsimulation scenarios, skill labs, and objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs). Read more Student Worker SLA MIT (TIER1) 492700 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States School of Liberal Arts Campus Employment Student worker These administrative positions may include all or some of the following duties: copying, filing, answering telephones, greeting visitors, data entry, creating documents, assisting with event planning, liasing with students, faculty and staff, creating flyers and forms, attending events, etc. These are entry-level jobs that do not require specialized skills or training and will require specific instructions and oversight. Read more Graduate Residential Coordinator (Tier 3) 492701 Manhattan, New York, United States Student Srvs Auxiliary Campus Employment Student worker This is a unique role for a current graduate student that provides the opportunity to enhance leadership, interpersonal, networking and communication skills in the Office of Residential Life. The Residential Coordinator will work closely with the professional staff to create and contribute to the enhancement of an on-campus living and learning environment conducive to student success.\nReporting to the Associate Director of Residential Life (AD), the Residential Coordinator is a part-time live-in position at Dorm34 under a 10-month contract from August 2026 to May 2027. Read more Student Worker - Peer Tutor 492348 New York, United States Center for Student Success Campus Employment Student worker This position provides for tutoring and academic support to fellow students. In their interactions, they model good student practices such as study and note-taking strategies, help their peers develop time management skills, and foster confidence and self-reliance. May conduct and lead group study and tutoring sessions in a variety of formats, such as Supplemental Instruction (SI) and Structured Learning Assistance (SLA). In this role, they encourage student success through engagement with a variety of academic resources. Read more Student Worker – Office of the Provost (TIER1) 492697 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Provost's Office Campus Employment Student worker The Academic Affairs Assistant positions will support various programs and departments within Academic Affairs. The role will offer general administrative support to the Academic departments and the Libraries. The exact responsibilities will differ slightly based on the needs of the hiring department and will be communicated by the hiring manager during the interview process. This position will provide the student with a wonderful opportunity to learn about Mercy University and Higher Education in general, while honing skills that will serve them well once they graduate and start their professional journey.\nThis role will require general office software application skills (Word, Excel, and Outlook email), strong communication skills, a willingness to learn, and a desire to be a team player.\nThese positions will vary between 12-15 hours a week, will pay NYS minimum wage, and will be in effect for the 2026-27 Academic Year. Read more Simulation Lab Assistant - Bronx-  LB4120 492671 Bronx, New York, United States School of Nursing Staff Staff Part-Time The Simulation Lab Assistant provides crucial operational, technical, and administrative support to the Simulation Center and the Director of Simulation. This role ensures the smooth daily operation of the nursing simulation labs, prepares high-fidelity and low-fidelity environments for student experiences, manages specialized inventory, and assists faculty and students during active simulation scenarios, skill labs, and objective structured clinical examinations (OSCEs). Read more Director of Advancement Performance- A00403 492696 Tarrytown, New York, United States Institutional Advancement Staff Staff Full-time The Director of Advancement Performance is a strategic, hands-on advancement professional responsible for managing a portfolio of major and leadership gift prospects while overseeing the execution of core fundraising programs. This role bridges frontline fundraising, annual giving, and general development outreach to drive philanthropic results and ensure efficient, data-informed advancement practices. Read more Assistant Volleyball Coach- VB3735 492672 Dobbs Ferry, NY, New York, United States Athletics Athletics/Coaching Staff Part-Time Mercy University's Athletics program is looking for a dedicated Assistant Volleyball Coach to join its competitive NCAA Division II program at the Dobbs Ferry campus. If you bring hands-on coaching experience and a genuine commitment to student-athlete development, this is a meaningful opportunity to contribute to a program that takes both athletic performance and academic success seriously. Read more Student Worker Mentee (Undergraduate) 492694 New York, United States Libraries, Inst Tech & Online Learn Campus Employment Library Student worker Library Student Mentees will perform the following duties:\n\nServe as the Library’s first point of contact, welcoming and assisting students, faculty, and staff with a consistently professional, service-oriented demeanor.\nCurate and sustain shelf integrity by organizing, shelving, and maintaining the cleanliness and navigability of assigned collections to established standards.\nExecute all front-desk/circulation transactions with precision and compliance to standard operating procedures, ensuring data accuracy and patron confidentiality.\nTriage, answer, and appropriately route inbound telephone inquiries; document messages and escalate issues per communication protocols.\nOperate multifunction devices to produce copies, scans, and faxes; verify output quality and resolve routine user issues.\nMonitor and replenish consumables (e.g., printer and copier paper) to maintain continuous service availability; log inventory changes as directed.\nProvide Tier-1 technical assistance for patrons (e.g., printing, scanning, account access), including basic troubleshooting and timely escalation.\nConsistently demonstrate reliability, sound judgment, and a positive, professional presence; model customer-service best practices under varying demand levels.\nMaintain a safe, orderly, and audit-ready circulation and office environment by cleaning, organizing, and restocking supplies throughout the shift.\nFulfill Interlibrary Loan (ILL) requests by locating materials, verifying bibliographic details, and assisting with packaging, labeling, and processing to meet shipment timelines.\n \n\nIn addition to circulation:\n\nEngage in structured, mentor-guided exploration of academic and career pathways; establish goals and reflect on progress through scheduled check-ins.\nTranslate on-the-job responsibilities into resume-ready competencies by collaborating with the mentor and librarians to identify transferable skills and career applications.\nComplete curated microlearning (videos, articles, activities) aligned to career development milestones; document takeaways and action steps.\nPartner with Career Services for tailored resume refinement and interview preparation, integrating feedback into a professional portfolio.\nAuthor a librarian-supported research guide on a self-selected topic, demonstrating information literacy, audience awareness, and effective resource curation. Read more Graduate Residential Coordinator (Tier 3) 492695 Manhattan, New York, United States Student Srvs Auxiliary Campus Employment Student worker This is a unique role for a current graduate student that provides the opportunity to enhance leadership, interpersonal,\nnetworking and communication skills in the Office of Residential Life. The Residential Coordinator will work closely with the\nprofessional staff to create and contribute to the enhancement of an on-campus living and learning environment conducive\nto student success.\nReporting to the Associate Director of Residential Life (AD), the Residential Coordinator is a part-time live-in position at\nDorm34 under a 10-month contract from August 2026 to May 2027.\nResponsibilities include:\nStaff supervision\nAssist the AD with the supervision and training of Resident Assistants (RAs) in the areas of programming, crisis\nresponse, collaboration, and campus culture\nParticipate in RA training in the winter and summer as well as supplemental in-services and professional development\nopportunities\nOversee Desk Attendants (DAs) and RAs in the absence of professional staff members\nStudent Development and Engagement\nProvide leadership and support to the residential community at Dorm34\nRegularly interact with students and provide availability both during the day and in the evening hours\nAct in an advising capacity and refer students to appropriate campus offices, services, and resources in accordance\nwith the Student Handbook and Residential Life policies\nFollow up with student concerns, act as a liaison to ensure timeliness of reporting and service completion\nAssist with health and safety inspections and roommate mediations\nCrisis Response\nServe in the duty in collaboration with other live in staff at Manhattan campus (approximately two weeks per month)\nRespond to incidents in a timely manner and report them in accordance with policy\nAttend staff trainings to adequately and appropriately respond to incidents\nOther\nAttend various meetings with campus stakeholders\nAssist with administrative processes, policies, and procedures\nAbility to travel between campuses Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 115 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 › Equal Opportunity Consistent with its obligations under the law, Mercy University will provide reasonable accommodation to any employee with a disability who requires accommodation to perform the essential functions of the job. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Categories Accounting Careers Technology Careers Education Careers Administration Careers Recruiting Careers Quick Links About Us Contact Us Contribute Privacy Policy Sitemap © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Mercy University . Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
